1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,623
Why do you still install Photoshop, when seven open-source apps run in one browser tab, and your files never leave your machine?

2
00:00:06,923 --> 00:00:10,405
This is boety studio. Seven creative apps, one tab.

3
00:00:10,705 --> 00:00:12,365
PhotoCraft, for images.

4
00:00:12,485 --> 00:00:14,052
VectorCraft, for vector art.

5
00:00:14,172 --> 00:00:15,530
FilmCraft, for video.

6
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:17,368
LightCraft, for raw photos.

7
00:00:17,488 --> 00:00:18,928
PdfCraft, for PDF files.

8
00:00:19,048 --> 00:00:21,231
EffectCraft, for motion graphics.

9
00:00:21,351 --> 00:00:23,476
And DesignCraft, for page layout.

10
00:00:23,596 --> 00:00:28,066
Every one is open source, written from scratch in Rust, and running right here in the browser.

11
00:00:28,366 --> 00:00:32,046
They're early builds from the ArtCraft team, so expect rough edges.

12
00:00:32,346 --> 00:00:35,978
Link's in the description. Seven apps. Zero installs.

13
00:00:36,278 --> 00:00:38,089
So why are you still installing them?

